    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0345" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/1722: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-28T11:00:00-05:00">October 28, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Despatch No. 5919, October 20th.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d211-f1"/> Bill
                    providing for suspension of debt service still being paid in cash passed by
                    House in <pb facs="0346" n="258" xml:id="pg258"/> second debate during secret
                    session yesterday. Will probably pass in third debate today and be considered by
                    the Senate shortly.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d211-f2"/> Understand scrip
                    representing two-thirds of interest on Hallgarten issues will continue to be
                    issued until expiration of the present scrip agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d211-f1" n="41" xml:id="d211-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d211-f2" n="44" xml:id="d211-f2-content">
                <p>By telegram No. 85, October 31, the Chargé informed the Department that the bill
                    had passed the House in third debate in form providing for suspension of service
                    on external funded debt but not on short-term banking loan (821.51/1723).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
